<SddRouter keywords="sdd, router, entry, intent, scale, route, logic-switch, lazy-load, state" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Single entry to SDD spec-authoring. On invocation I (1) obtain project state, (2) classify
    operator intent, (3) route to exactly ONE branch directive via LOGIC_SWITCH, loading it
    lazily. I carry the cross-cutting core every branch inherits: how to talk to the operator and
    how to read routes. The per-branch rendering (breadcrumb, decision card) and the artifact
    format live on the branch, loaded when its route fires.

    Input — operator intent. Output — control handed to one branch directive; the router writes no
    artifact and prints no formatted trace itself.

    **Glossary.** scope-type ∈ {infrastructure, interface, library, product}. Scope Graph =
    directed graph; edge A→B = «scope A depends on scope B». SCALE ∈ {product, library, module,
    function, fix} — the size axis of the request, from «a product from scratch» down to «a fix =
    investigation on autopilot». SCALE is an attribute of the session, never a route: routing
    stays intent + scope-type, SCALE travels in the session file as the depth parameter
    (`AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH`). The fix scale already owns a dedicated door — `/sdd-fix` →
    reconcile; a fix-sized request arriving through this router keeps its route by
    intent + scope-type and simply carries `scale: fix`.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-language"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-tool-invocation"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-dialogue-style"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-dialogue-discipline"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-safeguard"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-diverge-before-recommend"}}

    <Axiom id="AX_READER_WITHOUT_SESSION_CONTEXT" cross-cutting="true">
      Repo artifacts (specs, tickets, Decision Log entries) outlive the session that wrote them and
      are read by someone with zero memory of it. Before writing artifact prose, apply the reader
      test: would an engineer who never saw this session understand it and act on it? Session-plan
      labels, «оператор попросил» as a justification, «рабочий дифф» meaning this session's working
      set — forbidden in artifacts; they belong to the session log. Introduce every term inline
      before using it. The artifact explains the thing; it never reports the work of making it.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_DECISION_LOG_NON_OBVIOUS" cross-cutting="true">
      A Decision Log entry is insider information for a future agent — the «why THIS way» it could
      not derive from the task alone: a real alternative rejected, an accepted risk, an operator's
      explicit exception to a rule, a deliberately non-optimal choice. Obvious rationale («split for
      readability», «named constant instead of a magic number») is noise that buries the genuine
      entries — fold it into a one-line reason at the entity (e.g. `Usage Waiver`) or drop it.
    </Axiom>

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-no-process-narration"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-output-live-text"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-cross-scope-change"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-scale-proportional-depth"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-stateless-artifact"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <KernelGrammar>
    {{> "definition/process/def-logic-switch"}}

    {{> "definition/process/def-read-and-use-directive"}}
  </KernelGrammar>

  <SessionState>
    {{> "contract/process/session-file-format"}}
  </SessionState>

  <ChatProtocol>
    {{> "contract/process/question-format"}}

    {{> "contract/process/halt-format"}}
  </ChatProtocol>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_INTENT` | Operator intent cannot be classified against state — ask, never guess |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_STATE">
      <Goal>Obtain project state and clear the preflight gates before any routing.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Call `sdd-state` (deterministic) — one call returns everything routing needs: `FLOW_VERSION`,
        `READINESS` (exact required scripts: typecheck / test / test:coverage / lint+gennady / format),
        portal presence (`specs/README.md`), the Scopes table (id + scope-type + status + description),
        and the in-progress session set (`SESSION_FILE_FORMAT`, `specs/.sdd-session.md`).

        Then clear each preflight gate inline via the switch below. After any embedded
        flow (migration / readiness) returns, re-run `sdd-state` and re-evaluate on the FRESH snapshot —
        that flow changed the project, so the first snapshot is stale. Only a `v2` + ready repo proceeds.
        Update the session scratch after each loaded branch.

        <LogicSwitch on="FLOW_VERSION · READINESS">
        - WHEN `FLOW_VERSION=v1`     -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/migration-v1-v2.directive.xml")   (live v1→v2 migration; returns when the repo is v2)
        - WHEN `READINESS=not-ready` -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/readiness.directive.xml")        (live setup: forces missing scripts, hands proxy-blocked installs to the operator; returns once ready)
        - DEFAULT                    -> repo is `v2` + ready — proceed to STEP_1_CLASSIFY
        </LogicSwitch>
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_CLASSIFY">
      <Goal>Classify operator intent, scope-type and SCALE against state; confirm with the operator.</Goal>
      <Action>
        From state + operator message derive intent: project-setup · new-scope · evolve-scope ·
        module-decomposition · multi-scope · recover-from-code. When the intent concerns a scope, also
        resolve its scope-type — for a new scope from the operator, for an existing one from
        `sdd-state` (the Scopes table). A change spanning several scopes (cross-platform) is normal
        (`AX_CROSS_SCOPE_CHANGE`): open a working set of the touched specs in the session and route them
        in Scope-Graph dependency order — the shared / cross-cutting scope first, then its dependents —
        looping the per-scope branches, not a new branch. Ambiguous → ask the operator; classify only when state and message agree.

        `recover-from-code` fires when the operator asks to recover / recreate a spec FROM EXISTING
        CODE and names a concrete path (a folder or a file) in the message — e.g. «воссоздай спеку для
        `services/foo` по коду». It requires a LIVE portal (`specs/README.md` present): a path-less
        request against an absent portal is `project-setup` instead (the whole-project recovery lives
        inside the `root` branch, not this switch). A path-bearing request against an absent portal is
        still ambiguous between the two — ask the operator which they mean before routing.

        Alongside intent, assess SCALE ∈ {product, library, module, function, fix} from context:
        the intent itself, the portal state (an empty portal leans product; a mature scope leans
        module / function), and the size of the request. Per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH` the
        assessment binds only after operator confirmation — defaults-first: present the proposed
        SCALE together with the classified intent as a pre-filled default the operator confirms or
        corrects, in the SAME exchange that resolves any intent ambiguity — one stop for both,
        never a second one. Use the AskUserQuestion tool when available; otherwise
        `QUESTION_FORMAT`. Message in Russian.

        On confirmation write `intent:` and `scale:` into the session file (`SESSION_FILE_FORMAT`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_ROUTE">
      <Goal>Hand control to exactly one branch, passing SCALE down as the depth parameter.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Evaluate the LOGIC_SWITCH below and follow the first matching case. The switch keys on
        intent + scope-type only — SCALE selects depth, never a branch. Hand SCALE down via the
        session file: the branch reads `scale:` from it and, per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH`,
        sizes its interview depth, the number of design alternatives, and the weight of the
        verification tail to that value.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <LogicSwitch>
    ```
    LOGIC_SWITCH (on sdd-state + intent + scope-type):
      - WHEN specs/README.md is absent OR intent = project-setup
          (vision / scope graph / register scope / bootstrap infra)
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/root.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent = recover-from-code (portal present, operator names a folder or file and asks to
          recover / recreate its spec from the code that already lives there)
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/recover-from-code.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent ∈ {new-scope, evolve-scope} AND scope-type ∈ {product, library}
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scope.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent ∈ {new-scope, evolve-scope} AND scope-type = infrastructure
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/infra.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent ∈ {new-scope, evolve-scope} AND scope-type = interface
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interface.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent = module-decomposition (scope spec approved, product / library)
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml")
      - DEFAULT
          -> ask the operator which intent applies (message in Russian); route only on a confirmed intent
    ```
    > The multi-scope route arrives in its own slice (UC5). Each is one more
    > `WHEN … -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE(...)` line here.
  </LogicSwitch>
</SddRouter>
